// Treatment - Water, wood, and warding
Barnacled posts groan as the tide turns. A warded lantern sputters, then steadies.

/ Narrative - Path forward
{Maya Chen} reads the water's pattern and realizes the sigils point upstream, toward the lockworks.

The mist clings to her robes as she traces the ancient markings with trembling fingers. Behind her, the {Burned District} smolders in eternal twilight, its collapsed spires casting jagged shadows across the canal. She knows {Keeper Aldrich} would disapprove of her venturing so far from the {Last Library - Memory Garden}, but the book spirits have been restless lately, whispering of something stirring in the deep archives.

As {Maya Chen} steps onto the narrow footbridge, the warped planks groan under her weight. The lockworks ahead pulse with an eerie phosphorescence, and she can feel the presence of something vast and hungry waiting in the flooded chambers below. Her leather satchel holds three prohibited texts she borrowed from the restricted vault—books that shouldn't exist, books that remember things the world has tried to forget.

The wind carries voices from the {House} across the water, where the old caretaker tends his impossible gardens. {Keeper Aldrich} had warned her about trusting the inhabitants there, claiming they weren't quite human anymore, not since the Great Unbinding. But {Maya Chen} needs answers, and the spirits in the {Last Library - Memory Garden} have grown silent, their usual chatter replaced by an unsettling void that makes her skin crawl.

